From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:11:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: ilp32: allow ARM64_PTR_AUTH

ARM64_ILP32 depended on !ARM64_PTR_AUTH. The dependency came with the
OLK-5.10 port of the series, without a reason given (norov/ilp32-5.2 did
not have it), and a configuration with pointer authentication silently
lost ILP32. What breaks is the build: with ARM64_PTR_AUTH_KERNEL the
kernel is built with -mbranch-protection=pac-ret, and GCC does not support
return address signing with -mabi=ilp32, so the ILP32 vDSO fails with
"return address signing is only supported for -mabi=lp64".

- vdso-ilp32: drop the return address signing flags of the kernel. With
  ARM64_BTI_KERNEL the vDSO pages are mapped as guarded pages, so keep the
  BTI landing pads there (-mbranch-protection=bti); otherwise
  -mbranch-protection=none.
- pointer_auth.c: PR_PAC_RESET_KEYS, PR_PAC_SET_ENABLED_KEYS and
  PR_PAC_GET_ENABLED_KEYS (and the NT_ARM_PAC_ENABLED_KEYS regset) refuse
  only AArch32 tasks: is_a32_compat_thread(). ILP32 tasks run AArch64 code
  with the PAC instructions. exec now also enables the keys of an ILP32
  task explicitly: ptrauth_thread_init_user() goes through
  ptrauth_set_enabled_keys(), which returned -EINVAL for ILP32 and left
  the keys of the previous program.
- Kconfig: drop the dependency.

The kernel keeps the user registers 64-bit (signal frames, ptrace
regsets), so signed return addresses of ILP32 code survive signals and
ptrace. GCC-built ILP32 programs have no PAC instructions; clang emits
pac-ret for ILP32.

Tested on QEMU -cpu max (FEAT_PAuth, FEAT_FPAC) with ARM64_PTR_AUTH,
ARM64_PTR_AUTH_KERNEL and ARM64_BTI: ILP32 (clang -mbranch-protection=
pac-ret, and GCC) and LP64 programs sign and authenticate, a wrong
modifier traps, the keys are kept over fork and new after exec, the
prctls and the NT_ARM_PAC_MASK and NT_ARM_PAC_ENABLED_KEYS regsets work,
and signed return addresses work through calls, signal handlers and
longjmp. ARM64_BTI_KERNEL needs clang and was not tested.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/Kconfig                    |  1 -
 arch/arm64/kernel/pointer_auth.c      |  6 +++---
 arch/arm64/kernel/vdso-ilp32/Makefile | 11 +++++++++++
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/Kconfig
@@ -1779,7 +1779,6 @@ config ARM64_TAGGED_ADDR_ABI
 
 config ARM64_ILP32
 	bool "Kernel support for ILP32"
-	depends on !ARM64_PTR_AUTH
 	help
 	  This option enables support for AArch64 ILP32 user space.  ILP32
 	  is an ABI where long and pointers are 32bits but it uses the AARCH64
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/pointer_auth.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/pointer_auth.c
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ int ptrauth_prctl_reset_keys(struct task
 	if (!system_supports_address_auth() && !system_supports_generic_auth())
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (is_compat_thread(task_thread_info(tsk)))
+	if (is_a32_compat_thread(task_thread_info(tsk)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (!arg) {
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ int ptrauth_set_enabled_keys(struct task
 	if (!system_supports_address_auth())
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (is_compat_thread(task_thread_info(tsk)))
+	if (is_a32_compat_thread(task_thread_info(tsk)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if ((keys & ~PR_PAC_ENABLED_KEYS_MASK) || (enabled & ~keys))
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@ int ptrauth_get_enabled_keys(struct task
 	if (!system_supports_address_auth())
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (is_compat_thread(task_thread_info(tsk)))
+	if (is_a32_compat_thread(task_thread_info(tsk)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (tsk->thread.sctlr_user & SCTLR_ELx_ENIA)
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/vdso-ilp32/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/vdso-ilp32/Makefile
@@ -50,6 +50,17 @@ ifneq ($(c-gettimeofday-y),)
   CFLAGS_vgettimeofday-ilp32.o += -include $(c-gettimeofday-y)
 endif
 
+# The return address signing flags of the kernel (ARM64_PTR_AUTH_KERNEL) are for LP64 code: GCC does not
+# support return address signing with -mabi=ilp32. Keep the BTI landing pads when the vDSO pages are
+# mapped as guarded pages (ARM64_BTI_KERNEL).
+CFLAGS_REMOVE_vgettimeofday-ilp32.o += -mbranch-protection=pac-ret+bti -mbranch-protection=pac-ret \
+				       -msign-return-address=non-leaf
+ifeq ($(CONFIG_ARM64_BTI_KERNEL),y)
+  CFLAGS_vgettimeofday-ilp32.o += -mbranch-protection=bti
+else
+  CFLAGS_vgettimeofday-ilp32.o += $(call cc-option,-mbranch-protection=none)
+endif
+
 # Clang versions less than 8 do not support -mcmodel=tiny
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_CC_IS_CLANG), y)
   ifeq ($(shell test $(CONFIG_CLANG_VERSION) -lt 80000; echo $$?),0)
